{"text": "CITY OF EL MONTE\nCITY CLERK\u2019S OFFICE\n\nGriselda Contreras,\nDeputy City Clerk /\nRecords Manager\n\nJuly 10, 2019\n\nVIA ELECTRONIC MAIL\nLouise Matsakis\n\n76404-68567905@requests.muckrock.com\n\nRe: _ Extension of Response Period Concerning Your Public Records Request\nReceived by the City of El Monte on July 1, 2019 ~\u2014 PRR #270\n\nDear Louise Matsakis,\n\nReference is made to your attached California Public Records Act request (the\n\u201cRequest\u2019), which was received by the City of El Monte (the \u201cCity\u201d) on July 1, 2019.\n\n\u2018As you know, Califoria Government Code Section 6253 generally requires local\nagencies to respond to a California Public Records Act request within ten (10) days\nfrom the receipt of the request. However, certain circumstances set forth in California\nGovernment Code Section 6253(c)(1-4) allow local agencies to extend the ten-day\nresponse period for up to fourteen (14) additional calendar days.\n\nIn accordance with California Government Code Section 6253(c)(2), the City requires\nfourteen (14) calendar days in addition to the ten-day response period in order to initially\nrespond to the Request as City staff needs to search for and examine a large number of\nrecords. City staff anticipates that its initial response to the Request shall be dispatched\non the fourteenth day of extension, which shall set forth the City's determination as to\nwhether the Request, in whole or in part, seeks copies of disclosable public records in\nthe City\u2019 s possession\n\nShould you have any questions or need any additional information, please do not\nhesitate to contact my office at (626) 580-2016, Monday through Thursday between the\nhours of 7:00 a.m. to 5:30 p.m.\n\nSincerely,\n\nKarina Casas\nOffice Assistant\n\n11333 VALLEY BOULEVARD, EL MONTE, CALIFORNIA 91\nEMAIL: ctvelerkalelmontera.gov WEBS!\n\n293 | (626) 580-2016 / FAX (626) 575.2274\new elmonteca.gov",
